{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` prior sampling statements for `sigma_a` and `sigma_y`, which are already finite-bounded parameters in the original model. The priors are placed before those parameters are used, satisfying SafeStan's unique-prior and before-use requirements. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] a;
  real mu_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[county[i]];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  a ~ normal(10 * mu_a, sigma_a);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
generated quantities {
  real<lower=0> s_a;
  real<lower=0> s_y;
  vector[N] e_y;

  e_y = y - y_hat;
  s_a = sd(a);
  s_y = sd(e_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":3,"county":[1,1,1],"y":[3.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
